<title>GREECE: BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS MORTGAGE RATE.</title>
<headline>BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS MORTGAGE RATE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Cyprus cut its drachma floating-rate mortgages by 190 basis points down to 12.0 percent effective June 9, setting the lowest rate in the market, it said.</p>
<p>The bank said borrowers may take advantage of a flexible mortgage product which offers partial or full early retirement without penalties.</p>
<p>Moreover, borrowers may take out foreign currency loans at rates which start from 5.7 percent.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
